  <content>
  <section><para>In this unit, students will: </para>
<list>
  <item> Write systems of two linear equations and solve the systems by graphing, substitution, and elimination. </item>
  <item> Solve linear inequalities in one and two variables. </item>
  <item> Graph the solution set of linear inequalities in two variables and systems of two linear inequalities in two variables on the coordinate plane. </item>
</list>
<para>To accomplish these unit-level learning goals, students will complete the following lessons and activities.</para>
<title>Student Readiness for Unit 2</title>
<para>To be ready for this unit, students will need to be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Determine if an ordered pair is a solution to a linear equation. </item>
  <item> Work with slope-intercept form of a linear equation. </item>
  <item> Find the \(x\)- and \(y\)-intercepts of a line when given its equation. </item>
</list>
<para>This Unit Overview Video will provide a big picture look at the content found in this unit as well as the prerequisite skills that students need for accessing the content in the unit.</para><div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-justify-content-center">
  <iframe><iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/bng5LyEIoSg;&amp;rel=0" title="YouTube video player"/></iframe>
</div>
